{% if r.baseline_change %}<div class="callout" role="note"><p><b>New test baseline from {{ r.baseline_change.start }}.</b> {{ r.baseline_change.why }} This run is not a like-for-like comparison with {{ r.baseline_change.prev_date }}: the agents themselves changed, so a lower score can come from a newer agent handling an add-on differently or from the new test machine, not necessarily from the add-on breaking.</p>
<ul>{% for a in site.agents %}{% if r.baseline_change.to[a] %}<li>{{ a|agentName }}: <code>{{ r.baseline_change.from[a] }}</code> → <code>{{ r.baseline_change.to[a] }}</code></li>{% endif %}{% endfor %}</ul>
<p>{{ r.baseline_change.pass_to_fail }} installs that passed on {{ r.baseline_change.prev_date }} failed on the new setup and {{ r.baseline_change.fail_to_pass }} went the other way. We mark the new failures pending and re-check them on the new setup; nothing is called "broke" or "fixed" across the switch.{% if runNotes.no_valid_run.length %} There is no valid run for {% for n in runNotes.no_valid_run %}{{ n.date }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %} (a test-harness bug, fixed; see <a href="/reports/#no-valid-run">the reports list</a>).{% endif %}</p></div>
{% elif r.baseline and r.baseline.recent %}<div class="callout" role="note"><p><b>New test baseline since {{ r.baseline.start }}:</b> newer releases of all 5 agents ({% for a in site.agents %}{% if r.baseline.to[a] %}{{ a|agentName }} {{ r.baseline.to[a] }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}). Scores before {{ r.baseline.start }} came from older agent versions and are not like-for-like. "Confirmed broke" and "really fixed" only compare nights on the same baseline. <a href="/reports/{{ r.baseline.start }}/">What changed</a></p></div>{% endif %}
